** Session 4: The Watch Gets Whacked **



   Back in the game. I'm anxious to see how my new dagger skill works.
<anticipation>

   Heading along the darkened corridor towards, what I undoubtedly
know, is Temple Town.

   Along comes a watchman. My eyes light up. Here is an opportunity to
improve my armor class (at the expense of this elf's life)...

< You kill the watchman! > 

T:3109

   Great! He had a shield, gloves, and shoes. I scoop them up and
enter the town. I'm looking for the temple, so as to test my new booty
for cursedness.

< You throw two daggers. The 1st dagger hits the grid bug. You kill
the grid bug! The 2nd dagger hits the grid bug. You kill the grid bug!
>

T:3113

   My first double killing this game! <grin>

< You throw two daggers. The 1st dagger hits the kobold lord. The 2nd
dagger hits the kobold lord. You kill the kobold lord! >

T:3123

   My first slaying of a kobold lord this game! <grin>

   Thirty turns in so far, and look at what I've accomplished already!
I think I'm on a role. <big grin>

   Got to the altar in the temple. Was a temple to Thoth (neutral), by
the way. <shrug> Just means I have added something new on my 'Things
To Do' list... <wink>

   I snubbed the priest (that's right - it wasn't a priestess) of
Thoth, and dropped my loot. None of my booty was cursed. I hurriedly
don the new apparel, and looked at the various screens...

AC:2 Fail 13% (for Force Bolt) T:3194

   Good enough. I'm more than satisfied with those statistics.

   Now what's in the shops...?

   Closest was; Renrut's Hardware Store.

Fine goods for sale:

a yellowish brown gem, 1333 zorkmids
a lock pick, 26 zorkmids
a large box, 10 zorkmids
a key, 17 zorkmids
a key, 13 zorkmids
a key, 13 zorkmids
a brass lantern, 16 zorkmids
a tin opener, 40 zorkmids
a whistle, 17 zorkmids
a stethoscope, 100 zorkmids

T:3280

   Oh sweet Lord! 

   My jaw drops, and my mouth hangs open. This guy has a treasure
trove!

   Lock pick, large box, brass lantern, (maybe the) whistle, and a
stehtescope.

   I'm still gawking at the screen. As I manage to tear my eyes away
from his inventory, my mind immediately starts to work on how I can
kill this guy.

   Is this a wonder whistle? Nope. It made a high sound. I named
(called) it "high", before dropping it back.  Allright then, next:
Let's see what we're up against. I don't care if it's cursed, or not.
I pick up the stehtescope and try it (apply) on Renrut.
 
   Mmmmkay... I decide against killing him - for now. I'll see what
else is in town, and start planning on what; to buy, steal, who to
murder, etc., when I have all the information. Who knows? There may be
a wand of death over in another store.

   I drop it back onto the pile and take a step outside. My mind is
still focused on this guy's inventory - and how I can acquire it -
when...

   The message screen fills up with a whole slew of attacks on Elryk!

T:3290 

   Yikes! A quasit and five wolves are after me! (Why is a quasit
after me any way? They're chaotic, thus should be peaceful.)

   Trying to run towards Misericorde; firing as I go...

T:3294

< The dagger hits the quasit! > 

   I marked this in time, because it was the first "!" I got with
daggers. I'm still trying to understand what they (the exclamation
marks) signify exactly.

T:3329 

   Killed the quasit, and a wolf with force bolts. I'm hurting. Almost
with my cat though.

T:3333 

   Down to 15 hit points. I'm cornered. Zapping the wand of sleep
(Yes, that is correct. First time, since the beginning of the game,
that I had to use it.).

   Oh no! I hit the wolf, which was at point blank range, but the ray
kept on going and nailed the watch captain who was at range 8! He's
pissed. And now heading for me! Crap! Crap! Crap! (Although I didn't
think about this at the time, I would remember this particular
sequence for later on...)

T:3399 

   Misericorde's been doing a wonderful job. But she can't take down a
wolf quickly enough. And I can never remember which wolf is asleep. I
had to zap a wolf that was in direct line of sight with her. So she's
out too. (I'm) Down to 8 hit points. Watch captain is at range two.
I'm getting pretty desperate. I know that the sleep wand won't work on
him - he's an elf. So, I'm gonna try this iridium mystery wand on
him...

  "Z"

   He disappeared! I sure hope it wasn't a wand of make invisible!!!

T:3441 

   No sign of the watch captain. And haven't been attacked by anything
that's invisible. It has to be a teleportation wand. From what I've
seen it do, I just can't recall that it could possibly be anything
else (?). Another wolf has just stepped next to me. I've been timing
the whole battle with the clock ticks. I'm sure I have a free round.
So I zap the mystery wand on me...

T:3442 

   It's teleport! <huge sigh of relief>

   Okay. I wait for my heart to slow down...

   What an immediate and intense fight! 

   I was just minding my own business, contemplating on whether to
murder a shopkeeper or not, then all of a sudden; I'm in a running
battle - where I got cornered by strong foes!

   Welcome to Nethack!

   Now then: I go into hunting mode. I hear noises in the distance.
Misericorde is probably finishing off the wolves. I'm not worried
about her. More important things to concentrate on now. I have some
new business - and an immediate new mission - to take care of...

< You kill the watch captain! Welcome to experience level 8. >

Elryk the Thaumaturge  St:7 Dx:16 Co:16 In:18 Wi:8 Ch:8  Chaotic
Dlvl:7  $:0  HP:30(67)  Pw:29(92)  AC:2  Exp:8  T:3513

   Now for the rest of these guys. While I'm at it; I'll whack the
whole lot. The more I think about it; they're just annoyances that
always tend to get in the way of what my characters want to do... <ice
cold leer>

< You kill the watchman! >

T:3583 

   That was the last of them. The town watch has been dispatched. <two
thumbs up!>

   Another long session. <slump shoulders> I don't feel like
collecting all the booty right now. I'll do it tomorrow. Signing off
for the night.

